STAR/FOLD native media previews

STAR/KIT dynamically links FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org), including
libavcodec, libavformat, libavutil, libavfilter, libswscale and libswresample.
The media player is native Rust; FFmpeg supplies codecs and conversion.

Most FFmpeg code is licensed under LGPL 2.1 or later; the license text is in
LICENSES/ffmpeg-LGPL-2.1.txt. FFmpeg builds enabling GPL components, including
libx264 used for the SSH H.264 preview, are governed by the corresponding GPL
terms. Dynamically linked binary distributions inherit the linked build's
applicable terms. Application sources remain available in this repository.

Nix and Arch use their distribution's FFmpeg. AppImages bundle Debian's shared
libraries in usr/lib, replaceable with compatible libraries without rebuilding
STAR/FOLD. macOS archives require Homebrew FFmpeg. Sources for these libraries
are available from https://ffmpeg.org/download.html and the supplying
package distribution. See FFmpeg's LICENSE.md for component-specific terms.

Bundled PDF preview extension

starfold-preview-pdf uses Hayro 0.8.0 (https://github.com/LaurenzV/hayro),
licensed under MIT or Apache-2.0. Its embedded standard fonts, character maps
and color data carry the notices installed as LICENSES/Hayro-*.txt.
Hayro is isolated in the PDF executable; it is not linked into STAR/FOLD.

Archive extension and native codecs

starfold-archive is a separate, replaceable executable. Its archive engines
are not linked into STAR/FOLD. Rust/C++ codec notices include UnRAR.txt.
Zstandard encoding uses Zstandard 1.5.7, distributed under its BSD license;
source: https://github.com/facebook/zstd/tree/v1.5.7 .

Native 7-Zip: Copyright (C) 1999-2026 Igor Pavlov. Source and component terms:
https://github.com/ip7z/7zip . LICENSES/Archive-7zip.txt includes its notice;
LGPL 2.1 terms are also installed as ffmpeg-LGPL-2.1.txt. AppImages use Debian's
p7zip executable/plugin; their corresponding sources are available from
https://sources.debian.org/src/p7zip/ . Nix uses its pinned 7-Zip package and
Arch/Homebrew use the supplying distribution's codec package.

XADMaster / unar: https://github.com/MacPaw/XADMaster/tree/v1.10.8 .
LICENSES/Archive-XAD.txt supplies its license. Sources for AppImage's shared
libraries and unar are available from https://sources.debian.org/src/unar/ and
https://sources.debian.org/ . Native codec binaries and their shared libraries
remain replaceable. Nix retains store dependencies; Arch/macOS use separately
installed runtime codec packages. Their licenses do not change the MIT license
of FOLD or the archive protocol/client code.
